    "recommendations": "Reducing the density and continuity of shrub and brush cover in the immediate area surrounding the structure should be a primary focus, as breaking up the continuous connection between vegetation and the building could meaningfully reduce fuel continuity and improve defensible space around the structure. Thinning or removing brush that is in direct contact with or immediately adjacent to the structure would support suppression operations and may reduce structure exposure. Creating and maintaining separation between scattered trees, tree clusters, and the underlying shrub layer could further reduce vertical fuel continuity. Along the long driveway, managing vegetation on both sides to maintain adequate width and clearance would support firefighter access and improve evacuation conditions. Sustaining these vegetation management efforts over time, particularly where dense shrub cover reestablishes seasonally, would contribute to long-term wildfire resilience and help maintain the property in a more defensible condition."
